# Node-side dev tests. rootDir is "." here and this list does not exclude JS by extension, so
# without this clasp pushes tests/*_test.js into the Apps Script project as .gs source — where it
# fails to parse and blocks the whole deploy. That is exactly what happened on 2026-08-22.
tests/
tests/**
**/*.html
!index.html
**/*.json
!appsscript.json
# .claude/ NEEDS ITS /** SIBLING, and for eleven months it did not have one. Every other directory
# entry in this file is listed twice — tests/ + tests/**, tools/ + tools/**, design_handoff_*/** —
# because the bare form does not exclude what is NESTED inside. .claude/ was the one exception, and
# it broke a deploy on 2026-09-16: a leftover preflight worktree at
# .claude/worktrees/.gxpreflight-*/serve.gs was pushed as Apps Script source, failed to parse, and
# blocked the ENTIRE deploy — a library re-pin that had nothing to do with it.
# Fourth instance of the one mechanism this file already explains three times: rootDir is "." and
# nothing here excludes by extension, so the first unparseable file in a new directory stops
# everything. The worktrees are live and were not deleted; they simply must not ship.
.claude/
.claude/**
clasp.sh
# Design handoff folders. Same failure mode as tests/ above: a stray .js in one of these gets pushed
# as .gs source and can break the whole deploy. Globbed, not named one by one — the period-selector
# folder was about to ship its support.js on 2026-08-25 because the list only knew the income one.
design_handoff_income_layout/**
design_handoff_*/**
**/*.jsx

# Node-side DEV SERVER, synced in from gx-theme on 2026-09-03 (commit bd7f5e2). Same failure mode as
# tests/ and design_handoff_*/ above and it fired the same way: rootDir is "." and nothing here
# excludes JS by extension, so clasp pushed serve.js as serve.gs, where `#!/usr/bin/env node` on
# line 1 is a parse error that blocks the ENTIRE deploy — backend fix and all. Not caused by any
# change to this app; it was armed the moment the file landed and would have stopped the next
# deploy whatever it carried.
serve.js

# Node/python diagnostics that run on a DEVELOPER's machine, never in Apps Script. Added with
# tools/exec_stall_probe.py (2026-09-16), which is .py and therefore not pushed by clasp today —
# this entry is for the next file in here. tests/, design_handoff_*/ and serve.js above are three
# instances of one mechanism: rootDir is "." and this list excludes nothing by extension, so the
# first .js anyone drops in a new directory ships as .gs and blocks the entire deploy. Listing the
# directory when it is created costs one line; finding out the other way costs a deploy.
tools/
tools/**
